      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The inability to advance a balloon across a chronically occluded coronary artery that has been crossed with a guidewire occurs in 5% of patients with chronic occlusions. In this report, a new indication for the excimer laser is described: the recanalization of a chronic occlusion that has been crossed with a guidewire that cannot be crossed with a balloon catheter."},
